ravi: Heads-up - our sample app using js-sdk@0.13.0 is failing on Cloudflare Workers. Retries are triggering but body becomes empty on the retried request.
ravi: Observed with streaming uploads and also when we wrap body in a ReadableStream. Works fine on node.
ravi: Error from backend: 'empty body' for second attempt. No errors surfaced in worker.
katie: Workers' fetch clones only support byte streams and some ReadableStream shapes. If the SDK retry tries to clone the Request and stream isn't tee()-able we'll get a drained body.
leo: can you paste the relevant retry logic? Might be using `new Request(req)` which clones; that fails for some stream bodies in wrangler.
ravi: snippet: ```js
async function sendWithRetry(req) {
  try {
    return await fetch(req);
  } catch (e) {
    // naive retry
    return await fetch(new Request(req));
  }
}
```
tia: naive cloning is the issue. On Cloudflare you need to either buffer the body (not ideal for large streaming requests) or design retry to be idempotent and only retry on safe methods / short bodies.
katie: also found sdk auth code uses `crypto.createHmac('sha256', secret)` in one place which blows up in Workers because `crypto.createHmac` is Node-only. That explains some crashes we saw earlier when auth header generation fails quietly.
leo: sounds like two separate but related DX problems: (1) retry + streaming compatibility, (2) node-crypto/Buffer assumptions.
ravi: proposal: ship an `edge` entrypoint (dist/edge.mjs) that: uses `globalThis.crypto.subtle` for HMAC, uses `btoa`/TextEncoder for base64, and exposes a `createRetryableRequest` util that marks bodies as bufferable or non-retryable.
tia: for retry util API idea: ```ts
// returns either a re-creatable factory or null if not retryable
function makeRequestFactory(req: Request): (() => Request) | null;
```
 tia: then SDK retry logic can call factory() to get fresh Request instead of cloning.
katie: also types: our current types reference `Buffer` in many places which makes TypeScript break in browser projects unless `skipLibCheck` is on. We should add `types/edge.d.ts` and change `package.json` to add an `exports` edge subpath.
leo: example package.json snippet: ```json
"exports": {
  ".": {
    "import": "./dist/index.mjs",
    "require": "./dist/index.cjs",
    "edge": "./dist/edge.mjs"
  },
  "./types": "./dist/types/index.d.ts"
}
```
katie: small behavioural note: bundlers might still pick the main export unless `conditions` include `edge` and runtime uses `import` conditions. We should document how to import explicitly: `import sdk from 'redwood-sdk/edge'` or `import { makeRequestFactory } from 'redwood-sdk/edge'`.
ravi: I opened a quick-fix branch that replaces `Buffer` and `createHmac` usages in the auth path with conditional polyfills and adds a `makeRequestFactory` fallback that buffers up to 1MB and returns null if larger. Tests added for wrangler/miniflare.
ci-bot: Created pipeline ticket devex/ci#7821 to add `miniflare` and `wrangler` stages into the matrix.
devex-bot: Suggested checklist: [ ] implement edge.mjs entry [ ] add makeRequestFactory util + docs [ ] replace Node crypto/Buffer in auth path [ ] add edge.d.ts types [ ] CI: run miniflare + wrangler tests
leo: can we add a runtime detection helper `isEdgeRuntime()` that uses `typeof WebSocket !== 'undefined' && typeof process === 'undefined'`? Might be brittle.
katie: prefer feature-detect: `const isEdge = typeof globalThis?.WebSocket !== 'undefined' && typeof globalThis?.crypto?.subtle !== 'undefined';`
ravi: good call. I'll open PR and request reviews from katie/leo/tia. Also will add migration note to sample app README explaining non-retryable streaming bodies and how to opt into buffering.
ria: thanks all, will follow the PR.
